       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg PO once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose.** The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. At 50 mg/day, the patient could develop severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so an overdose is hard to reverse quickly.\n\nThis may be a typo for **5 mg** (a common starting dose) or **10 mg**.\n\nCould you confirm which you meant?\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**\n- A different dose\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, please give me the clinical reason. I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy and nursing see it during their review."
